<title>UK: ING Barings sets warrants on Greek banking stocks.</title>
<headline>ING Barings sets warrants on Greek banking stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Baring Financial Products said it is launching $10.0 million of American-style call warrants, on Greek banking stocks. The banks included are Alpha Credit Bank, National Bank of Greece, Ergo Bank, Commercial Bank of Greece, National Mortgage Bank of Greece and Ionian Bank.</p>
<p>Sigma Securities S.A. will be acting as the Greek placing agent.</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE   $12.5		  EXPIRATION    ONE YEAR</p>
<p> LISTING	 LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p> NOTES	   ONE HUNDRED WARRANTS CONTROL $100.</p>
<p>		   THE WARRANT PREMIUM WILL BE PAYABLE IN DRACHMA</p>
<p>		   THE STRIKE PRICE WILL BE SET AT THE MONEY.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
